title: Paper
---
<<declare $takenPaper = false>>

There's a piece of paper on the floor. Do you take it?

-> Take it. <<if hasActions()>>
    <<jump PaperTaken>>
-> Crumple it up and take it. <<if hasActions()>>
    <<jump PaperCrumple>>
-> Leave
    <<stop>>
===
title: PaperTaken
---
<<useAction>>
<<PaperTook>>
<<set $takenPaper = true>>
You take the paper and carefully stow it away in your backpack.
<<stop>>
===
title: PaperCrumple
---
<<useAction>>
<<PaperCrumpleTook>>
<<set $takenPaper = true>>
You grab the paper and crumple it and stuff it into your pocket.
<<stop>>

===


title: Evidence
---
<<if getBool("hasEvidence")>>
    Nothing else to see here.
    <<stop>>
<<else>>
    Looking into the desk, you find a file named Opitz. Inside it shows he has 0 credits!

    -> Take the files. <<if hasActions()>>
        <<setBool "hasEvidence" true>>
    -> Don't take it.
        <<stop>>
<<endif>>
===

